-- title:
--   A detector cannot distinguish two detected points
-- statement:
--   Let $f$ be a continuous linear functional with $\|f\|\le1$, and $y,a,b$ vectors with $\|y-a\|\le1$, $\|y-b\|\le1$, $f(y-a)\ge1-e$ and $f(y-b)\ge1-e$. Then
--   $$
--   |f(a-b)|\le e .
--   $$
--
--   A functional that nearly norms both $y-a$ and $y-b$ nearly vanishes on $a-b$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Nonexpansive/BranchContradiction.lean#L25-L41

